                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d15bc26c-17db-4c72-8ebf-7dd202996ec8",
                                                "sense_id": "242eabde-7aa1-38c3-b24e-d22a343bedb1",
                                                "text": "His empty stomach was suddenly full of butterflies, and for the first time since arriving here at scenic Durkin Grove Village, he felt an urge to gag himself. He would be able to think more clearly about this if he just stuck his fingers down his throat […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08dc6ad6-1e87-3860-8484-130c3b18045d",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To restrain someone's speech by blocking his or her mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f189a71-d422-453d-8611-40c3b7cb89af",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc6ad6-1e87-3860-8484-130c3b18045d",
                                                "text": "“[…] Captain Markam had been found lying half-insensible, gagged and bound, on the floor of the sitting-room, his hands and feet tightly pinioned, and a woollen comforter wound closely round his mouth and neck ; whilst Mrs. Markham's jewel-case, containing valuable jewellery and the secret plans of Port Arthur, had disappeared. […]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e48f26ec-6ff2-4b7a-84fc-a009b10e13d3",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc6ad6-1e87-3860-8484-130c3b18045d",
                                                "text": "They said no word to the landlord, they drank his ale instead, / But they gagged his daughter and bound her to the foot of her narrow bed; / Two of them knelt at her casement, with muskets at their side!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ed1908d-1db1-3123-9e9c-9fdb335cfe60",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pry or hold open by means of a gag."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6341a1c1-228a-453a-ac2b-77aa8bab0058",
                                                "sense_id": "8ed1908d-1db1-3123-9e9c-9fdb335cfe60",
                                                "text": "1917, Francis Gregor (translator), De Laudibus Legum Angliae, Sir John Fortescue, written 1468–1471, first published 1543.\n[…] some have their mouths gagged to such a wideness, for a long time, whereat such quantities of water are poured in, that their bellies swell to a prodigious degree […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "653c00cc-957c-3664-b8be-850bd3b6a7fd",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To restrain someone's speech without using physical means."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a55f3d59-343b-4014-8748-6af563640a06",
                                                "sense_id": "653c00cc-957c-3664-b8be-850bd3b6a7fd",
                                                "text": "When the financial irregularities were discovered, the CEO gagged everyone in the accounting department."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce76c600-2b8b-4bc7-8830-73c20551e49d",
                                                "sense_id": "653c00cc-957c-3664-b8be-850bd3b6a7fd",
                                                "text": "The time was not yet come when eloquence was to be gagged, and reason to be hoodwinked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "019bc614-d9bd-4d1b-830f-eb39ea9905aa",
                                                "sense_id": "653c00cc-957c-3664-b8be-850bd3b6a7fd",
                                                "text": "Vaid blasted the Bush administration for gagging doctors from discussing abortion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2a4bf34-b878-3260-bbc4-c7028bf6563a",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To choke; to retch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19835fdb-d93c-3d71-a9ac-deaccf0fd61c",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deceive (someone); to con."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cb5af20-2b2e-4de6-92b3-0476dd696204",
                                                "sense_id": "19835fdb-d93c-3d71-a9ac-deaccf0fd61c",
                                                "text": "I endeavoured what I could to soften off the affectation of her sudden change of Disposition; and I gagged the Gentleman with as much ease as my very little ease would allow me to assume."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68ef5c34-d596-315e-8e75-2ee6c1a6c708",
                                        "entry_id": "356836f6-992d-3076-9fcc-aef8aac5795d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To astonish (someone); to leave speechless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27737138-2ed5-43c9-b1ca-75572a45741a",
                                                "sense_id": "68ef5c34-d596-315e-8e75-2ee6c1a6c708",
                                                "text": "I knew who you were as a [RuPaul's] Drag Race fan. So I was gagged personally and I still am gagged, but it was quite divine intervention. Thom Kerr, the photographer, really got the ball rolling and I had no idea what to expect of this shoot besides greatness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
